<title>JORDAN: Jordan overnight rates rise to 3.25-4.00 pct.</title>
<headline>Jordan overnight rates rise to 3.25-4.00 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight rates on the Jordanian dinar rose slightly on Tuesday to between 3.25 percent and 4.00 percent from 2.50 percent to 3.00 percent on Monday but the market remained flush with cash, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's still not much demand for dinars,&quot; one said.</p>
<p>Another dealer said banks with excess liquidity had been lending as low as 2.5 percent early on Tuesday.</p>
<p>$1 = 0.7080 dinar</p>
<p>-- Amman newsroom +962 6 623 776</p>
</text>
